  "content": {
    "id": "p60-q25-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "25",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the tangent to $h=(t+1)^2(t-1)^7$ at $(2,9)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$69t-h-129=0$",
      "worked": "Using the product and chain rules:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dh}{dt}&=2(t+1)(t-1)^7+7(t+1)^2(t-1)^6\\\\\\frac{dh}{dt}&=(t+1)(t-1)^6\\bigl[2(t-1)+7(t+1)\\bigr]\\\\\\frac{dh}{dt}&=(t+1)(t-1)^6(9t+5).\\end{align*}$$\nAt $t=2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}m&=(2+1)(2-1)^6(9\\cdot2+5)\\\\m&=69.\\end{align*}$$\nThe tangent through $(2,9)$ is\n$$\\begin{align*}h-9&=69(t-2)\\\\h&=69t-129\\\\69t-h-129&=0.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
